{"text": " There are six ways to get the same customer to pay you more money. First is obviously to increase price. So if fulfillment stays the same, then every dollar of price increase drops straight to the bottom line, which is good. Number two is you can decrease costs. So you decrease the cost of whatever it takes you to fulfill your product or service. Number three is you increase purchase frequency. Getting somebody to buy your product or service more times. Number four is upselling. Getting somebody to buy a bigger or better or premium version of whatever they just bought. Number five is cross-sell. Getting someone to buy an additional or complimentary product or service in addition to their original purchase. Number six is a down sell. So you sell a smaller, less expensive, less premium version of your main thing. This is a small slice of the taxes that we use to grow our portfolio company that generates over $250 million per year.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.8800000000000001, "text": " There are six ways to get the same customer", "tokens": [50364, 821, 366, 2309, 2098, 281, 483, 264, 912, 5474, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057062257419933, "compression_ratio": 2.019774011299435, "no_speech_prob": 0.000933751929551363}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 1.8800000000000001, "end": 3.0, "text": " to pay you more money.", "tokens": [50458, 281, 1689, 291, 544, 1460, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057062257419933, "compression_ratio": 2.019774011299435, "no_speech_prob": 0.000933751929551363}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 3.0, "end": 4.5200000000000005, "text": " First is obviously to increase price.", "tokens": [50514, 2386, 307, 2745, 281, 3488, 3218, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057062257419933, "compression_ratio": 2.019774011299435, "no_speech_prob": 0.000933751929551363}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 4.5200000000000005, "end": 5.76, "text": " So if fulfillment stays t